+# FlyWeb: release after 3.2.2 (softmac `seguridad/siguiente-3`), V8 fix 7be38d96f9 (crbug 585624821), the M156 merge of V8 15.6.75.81
+
+SEGURIDAD-PORTES-33, 24-11-2026 (softmac `FlyWeb/seguridad/siguiente-3/brave-core/0004`). M156 merge 7be38d96f9 (bugs
+589981130 and 585624821, main 9bbff6a346) on branch-heads/15.6, applied as is to 15.6.75.66. Severity not published.
+
+- `GraphReducer::Reduce` kept the `max_id` taken before the first reducer ran. If one reducer allocated new nodes (for
+  example the `ToBoolean` wrapper of an in-place `ReduceJSInstanceOf`) and a later reducer in the same step returned
+  `Replace(new_node)`, those new users stayed on the old node while its effect and control edges moved to the
+  replacement, leaving a broken graph in optimized code. `max_id` is now recorded before each reducer step, and
+  replacements made by an earlier reducer in the same step are reduced recursively.
+- `graph-reducer.cc` and `graph-reducer.h` are not touched by any other `patches/v8` file. Tests
+  `compiler/regress-585624821.js` and `compiler/regress-585624821-fast-api.js`.
+
+**Cache epoch:** covered by the single 40 -> 41 bump of `siguiente-3` (`brave-core/0001`).
+
+To check (D8-LINUX): mjsunit `compiler/regress-585624821*` and `compiler/*`.
+
